//api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T14:23:49Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T14:24:04Z","body":"Please make sure to escape `@final` with backticks or you will tag a user (same for all annotations)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991824294/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994230700","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722#issuecomment-2994230700","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107722","id":2994230700,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yeFWs","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-22T13:59:31Z","updated_at":"2025-06-22T13:59:31Z","body":"_Sorry for the little opinion piece here. The proposal is only about final methods so it doesn't seem to fit there._\r\n\r\nSome may think final classes are unnecessary in GDScript. I personally think we need this. Finality of class is an important property in the context of serialization. \r\n\r\nGodot's current approach to serialization (let's save the script path into the serialized data) is inherently unsuited for certain use cases like networking. An alternative approach often seen in other languages is serializing and de serializing with a given type. This approach can get complicated when it comes to polymorphism. Those problems (which are solvable but often user config is required for it) don't apply to final classes. Therefore, I think having the ability to mark classes as final is important for filling the secure object serialization gap that we currently have in Godot.\r\n\r\nHowever for this property to be useful in this context final classes would need to follow another restriction: They should not be attachable to sub types of the native type they extend. So a final class that extends from `Node` should not be attachable to `Node2D` IMO","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994230700/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994234764","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722#issuecomment-2994234764","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107722","id":2994234764,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yeGWM","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-22T14:07:12Z","updated_at":"2025-06-22T14:08:19Z","body":"> However for this property to be useful in this context final classes would need to follow another restriction: They should not be attachable to sub types of the native type they extend. So a final class that extends from `Node` should not be attachable to `Node2D` IMO\r\n\r\nThis can be accomplished in another pr imo. Currently let's complete the linguistic functionality to ensure the basic syntax is ready for being used in 4.6.\r\n\r\nBTW why the two Linux builds failed? I had no idea where the error originated.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994234764/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2996909184","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722#issuecomment-2996909184","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107722","id":2996909184,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yoTSA","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T15:21:38Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T15:22:20Z","body":"@Lazy-Rabbit-2001 If `@final` is implemented without the requirement @HolonProduction suggests, and then that requirement is added, it would break compatibility. Therefore, both need to be done in the same minor release, and it's worth having the discussion before merging this PR (though [the proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10500) would be better for @HolonProduction to mention this).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2996909184/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2997080582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722#issuecomment-2997080582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107722","id":2997080582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yo9IG","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T16:11:33Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T16:11:33Z","body":"See also my [comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10500#issuecomment-2298614390). In my opinion, `@final` is somewhat inconsistent with `@virtual` for methods (though it still makes sense for classes). I would prefer methods to be non-virtual by default. `@final` implies the opposite, you are forced to apply it to every method except the ones you want to make virtual, which is inconvenient in practice.\r\n\r\nOf course, we can't change this in 4.x for compatibility reasons, but we can introduce a warning, and users can change its level if they want. So, if I had to choose between `@final` and `@virtual`/`@override`, I would choose the latter. Can we have both? Probably yes, but I'm not sure it's a good idea.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2997080582/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015139565","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722#issuecomment-3015139565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107722","id":3015139565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zt2Dt","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-28T09:26:40Z","updated_at":"2025-06-28T09:26:40Z","body":"To keep the GDScript as simple and clean as it should be, sadly I have no choice but to close this pr.\r\nThanks for your support on this feature, but I don't think this is something really necessary for the gdscript. So keep it as clean as it should be.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015139565/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015153739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722#issuecomment-3015153739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107722","id":3015153739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zt5hL","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-28T09:57:21Z","updated_at":"2025-06-28T09:57:21Z","body":"In my opinion, you are a bit hasty in closing this PR. Personally, I think this is a good idea for classes (without going into the implementation details). Yes, one of the design goals of GDScript is simplicity and minimalism, but optional annotations do not seem too contradictory to me (of course, my opinion is not enough, discussion and review by the GDScript team is needed, as well as approval/consensus from the community on the proposal and PR).\r\n\r\nPerhaps you are frustrated that discussion and review take so much time? If so, do not think that there is something wrong with your PR. It is just that reviewing new features has a lower priority (especially during the feature freeze) than fixing bugs and regressions from other merged features. But if you really do not want to support this PR anymore, then I cannot ask you to work on it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015153739/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015157401","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722#issuecomment-3015157401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107722","id":3015157401,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zt6aZ","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-28T10:05:52Z","updated_at":"2025-06-28T10:16:05Z","body":"> In my opinion, you are a bit hasty in closing this PR. Personally, I think this is a good idea for classes (without going into the implementation details). Yes, one of the design goals of GDScript is simplicity and minimalism, but optional annotations do not seem too contradictory to me (of course, my opinion is not enough, discussion and review by the GDScript team is needed, as well as approval/consensus from the community on the proposal and PR).\r\n> \r\n> Perhaps you are frustrated that discussion and review take so much time? If so, do not think that there is something wrong with your PR. It is just that reviewing new features has a lower priority (especially during the feature freeze) than fixing bugs and regressions from other merged features. But if you really do not want to support this PR anymore, then I cannot ask you to work on it.\r\n\r\nNo, I just don't want to support such thing that has little improvement and is optional for a script.\r\nArchive it, plz","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015157401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]